# MemoDirector Environment Variables
# 
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Copy this file to .env: cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in your actual API keys below
# 3. Never commit the .env file to Git!

# ============================================
# LLM Provider Configuration (OPTIONAL - Development Only)
# ============================================
# These are ONLY used as fallback during development
# Users must add their own keys in: Profile → API Keys
# 
# For production deployment: Leave these empty or remove them
# For local development: Optional - add your test keys

# Google Gemini (Recommended - supports image/video generation)
# Get your key from: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_dev_key_here
# VITE_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash-exp

# OpenAI (GPT models)
# Get your key from: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY=your_dev_key_here
# VITE_OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# OpenRouter (Access to multiple models)
# Get your key from: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_dev_key_here
# VITE_OPENROUTER_MODEL=anthropic/claude-3.5-sonnet

# Ollama (Local LLM - no API key needed)
# Install from: https://ollama.ai
# VITE_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# VITE_OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2

# ============================================
# Supabase Configuration (REQUIRED for Multi-User)
# ============================================
# Get these from: https://supabase.com/dashboard/
# 
# Setup Steps:
# 1. Create a Supabase project
# 2. Go to Project Settings -> API
# 3. Copy the URL and anon/public key below

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url_here
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# ============================================
# IMPORTANT: API Keys are Now User-Managed
# ============================================
# AI provider API keys are NO LONGER set here!
# Users must add their own keys in the app:
# Profile → API Keys tab
# 
# This ensures:
# - User privacy (keys never sent to server)
# - User control (use their own keys)
# - Security (keys stored locally only)
# - Each user uses their own quota
# 
# PRODUCTION: Remove or leave empty
# DEVELOPMENT: Optional - for testing only
# 
# Priority: User keys (LocalStorage) > Environment variables
# If user has keys set, these are ignored.
